      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nanostructured coating may have a lower specific wear rate than the unchanged coating because of a lubricating oxide layer.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::022::4_conclusions",
        "PMC10820071::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxide layer formed on a worn surface under high load can lubricate the contact and reduce friction coefficient and specific wear rate.",
